Description: pvr: re-emit stream-out state after the indirect byte count program
 pvr_update_indirect_draw_byte_count_ext() emits its vertex count program as
 a stream-out sync state and then restored the previous stream-out shadow.
 The hardware state is the sync program at that point, but the shadow
 claimed the earlier stream-out program, so pvr_setup_stream_out() saw no
 change and did not send it again. A vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT after
 another draw in the same sub command then ran without the stream-out
 program, so it neither captured nor counted.
 .
 Leave the shadow cleared, as pvr_arch_emit_xfb_sync_state() does, so the
 next draw sends the stream-out words again.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
